{
  "abstract": "For connected symmetric nonnegatively weighted graphs with known positive decay and a cyclic signed port, local responses to continuous time inputs exist and have two derivatives at zero. In the separated-port spectral-band and contraction regime of Theorem A, equality of the first and half-mixed second terminal derivatives in all smooth compactly supported directions on one fixed positive horizon determines the source graph Laplacian and signed port up to the same vertex permutation. The admissible competitor can have any finite size. The spectral-band and contraction conditions apply to the source.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Mark Gladden"
    }
  ],
